  "term": "Research Diagnostic Criteria",
  "definition": "Research Diagnostic Criteria, in this context, refers to a standardized method used to identify temporomandibular disorders in research. It includes a physical examination component called Axis I and is used to classify these disorders, including muscular and degenerative forms.",
